{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes","id":1482849,"title":"Thumbs up or thumbs down these mechanic changes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-02T16:06:55-07:00","id":1482849,"title":"Thumbs up or thumbs down these mechanic changes","content":"(1)Stamina giving health levels instead of soak dice.<br /> <br /> (2)Difficulty being purely the number of 6+'s, rather than a combination of the difficulty being anything from 3+ to 10 and the number of successes.<br /> <br /> (3)The introduction of Hunger Dice and the resultant Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals.<br /> <br /> (4)Humanity based around 3 sins rather than a 1-10 chart.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T16:49:50-07:00","id":1482857,"title":"","content":"For my two cents, mostly thumbs down.<br /> <br /> 1. Health levels being almost always the same is part of the game balance, messing with that tends to very quickly skew things. While V:tM does sell itself on a social heavy play style, combat is too prevalent to ignore how quickly health level imbalance can change things.<br /> <br /> 2. I can see the value of attempting to simplify Difficulty, but in truth if the diff number goes below 6 then many people don't bother calling for a roll.<br /> <br /> 3. Never been a fan of those mechanics.<br /> <br /> 4. The paths have never been especially good guidelines IMO, reducing to down to three sins doesn't really improve the system, it just changes the degree to which the path matters in game, which in turn means if you are cutting it down by 70%, why not just ditch the entire system?<br /> <br /> Was that the sort of feedback you were after?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T17:04:09-07:00","id":1482861,"title":"","content":"Also, what's the starting point? The 1e and 2e base mechanics would interact differently with #2 and #3 than Revised or 20th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T17:45:31-07:00","id":1482870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes#post1482849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(1)Stamina giving health levels instead of soak dice.<br /> <br /> (2)Difficulty being purely the number of 6+'s, rather than a combination of the difficulty being anything from 3+ to 10 and the number of successes.<br /> <br /> (3)The introduction of Hunger Dice and the resultant Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals.<br /> <br /> (4)Humanity based around 3 sins rather than a 1-10 chart.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>(1) Seem interesting, but we would need something to soak damage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (2) I think the only good alternative is Requiem's approach.<br /> <br /> (3) Never liked these to begin with.<br /> <br /> (4) I think Humanity/Paths being reworked into something more interesting is a very promissing possibility, but the problem is to define &quot;How&quot;. Could you elaborate on that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T18:04:29-07:00","id":1482874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes?p=1482870#post1482870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> (4) I think Humanity/Paths being reworked into something more interesting is a very promissing possibility, but the problem is to define &quot;How&quot;. Could you elaborate on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand the question. This thread is about the canon changes from cwod, not me proposing homebrew.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T19:18:55-07:00","id":1482884,"title":"","content":"I also read that as backporting these things into a pre-V5 version of the game rather than, &quot;what do you think of these changes made for V5?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T19:26:45-07:00","id":1482885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes?p=1482884#post1482884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also read that as backporting these things into a pre-V5 version of the game</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no no no, that's not what I meant at all. I meant &quot;what do you think of these mechanical changes to vampire that we received this edition?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T19:50:36-07:00","id":1482886,"title":"","content":"Don't know if this is for comparing V5 to past editions or for backwards compatibility. Either or, here's my 2 cents.<br /> <br /> 1. In real life, different people are able to handle different levels of pain and injury. Both old and new represent this in different, but interesting ways. Ultimately, I prefer the old soak method.<br /> <br /> 2. No. While I appreciate V5 making &quot;difficulty&quot; fixed, it actually kind of made it worse in some ways. The old method of 3 to 9 is best honestly.<br /> <br /> 3. Mega no! While I love what hunger dice <b><i>try</i></b> to do, it actually kind of fails in practice. Hunger dice are not meant for systems where you roll often, which is ironic for a TTRPG. Also, fuck Messy Criticals specifically. They effectively turn an exceptional success into a botch!<br /> <br /> 4. Actually love this the most, although I'd personally make 1 change. Instead of calling it <b><i>Humanity</i></b> I'd call it <b><i>Integrity</i></b>. There wouldn't be much mechanical difference, except that Integrity is effectively flavored as one's conviction and control over oneself. Many vampires would still call it humanity, while others claim to follow their own paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T20:22:35-07:00","id":1482893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes?p=1482886#post1482886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4. Actually love this the most, although I'd personally make 1 change. Instead of calling it <b><i>Humanity</i></b> I'd call it <b><i>Integrity</i></b>. There wouldn't be much mechanical difference, except that Integrity is effectively flavored as one's conviction and control over oneself. Many vampires would still call it humanity, while others claim to follow their own paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I'd like that. The way I run it has distinct mechanical difference between following Humanity and following a Path. Humanity can have Touchstones in my games, whereas Paths can't have Touchstones.<br /> <br /> However, Path followers have Beast Marks appropriate to that Path. Beast Marks being flaws I took from &quot;Long Hard Road Out Of Hell&quot;, but modified to my needs. Whereas &quot;Long Hard Road Out Of Hell&quot; has Beast Marks for using non-human Touchstones, in my games Path followers get them simply for being on Paths, and can't have Touchstones of any sort.<br /> <br /> Following a Path is in some ways rough in my games. But you get the benefit of being able to follow Path Tenets, and Path Tenets are much more forgiving of the behaviors vampires perform in their nightly hunting and warring than Humanity is.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T21:47:23-07:00","id":1482898,"title":"","content":"OK, so with better clarity on the desired feedback:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes#post1482849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(1)Stamina giving health levels instead of soak dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thumbs up. Good fit for the general change in combat mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (2)Difficulty being purely the number of 6+'s, rather than a combination of the difficulty being anything from 3+ to 10 and the number of successes. </div> </div> </div>Also thumbs up. The older game had too many variables and something needs to go. Target numbers being set at X is the best of the options because it makes it much easier to understand the math of the game and how to value different adjustments. Needing to roll 7s instead of 6s for +1 dice of damage is not intuitive to understand if that's a good or bad deal. Taking a -1 dice penalty to inflict 1 damage is easier to see as, on average, a fairly good deal on average damage, but still tactically variable because of how V5 combat works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (3)The introduction of Hunger Dice and the resultant Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals. </div> </div> </div>Thumbs down. Hunger Dice are too present leading to Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals as too much of a constant risk regardless of the stakes of the scene. The justification the &quot;blood points are a boring gas tank,&quot; given by Martin I think loses both the utility of tracking set points over random outcomes,and how to connect the random outcomes effectively as consequence for other choices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (4)Humanity based around 3 sins rather than a 1-10 chart. </div> </div> </div>Hard to answer as I don't entirely agree on the premise of treating the three Chronicle Tenets as equivalent to the old sins charts (there are other ways to get stains that apply regardless of Chronicle Tenets).<br /> <br /> But to give some level of answer to the intended comparison: thumbs up to negotiated for the group chronicle &quot;morality&quot; as a tool to help get the group on the same page as to the moral themes that will be present in a given instance, but thumbs down to the implementation and specifically of how it interacts with the Stains system. Most specifically I find the guidance on how severe a Stain penalty should be very lacking. Once you get to &quot;how bad is this violation&quot;as a ST, you have incredibly broad fiat to interpret and assign Stains for the action, and the players have to trust you to be fair and fun in it and have minimal recourse in the text regarding best practices to point to if they have trouble with the call.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T21:52:55-07:00","id":1482900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes?p=1482886#post1482886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Actually love this the most, although I'd personally make 1 change. Instead of calling it <b><i>Humanity</i></b> I'd call it <b><i>Integrity</i></b>. There wouldn't be much mechanical difference, except that Integrity is effectively flavored as one's conviction and control over oneself. Many vampires would still call it humanity, while others claim to follow their own paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Politicians would need to take an Integrity of 0, assuming that had humanity to begin with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T22:36:33-07:00","id":1482902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes?p=1482900#post1482900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Politicians would need to take an Integrity of 0, assuming that had humanity to begin with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Have you heard of the Path of Power and Inner Voice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T02:32:16-07:00","id":1482911,"title":"","content":"1) Speeds things up. I think VtR showed the advantages of this quite along time ago. The lack of random variables has a downside, but also an upside. <br /> <br /> 2) This is good. Low target number was always preferable and it was not obvious for everyone how the math worked. Now everything is more equal. I like target number 6 more than 8 simply because it generates more success, which clicks gratification in my head. I think the VtR system is more solidly designed, but a target number of 8 was always a really tough thing in older VtM, so I do not like it.<br /> <br /> 3) It is a hit and miss. Hunger is a simple yet much better system. Messy critical and beastly failures, well\u2026 That quickly goes into house rule territory. This could have been done better, but the fixes are so easy.<br /> <br /> 4) Absolutely fantastic. The old humanity was such a contrived mess. Breaking someone\u2019s bones was typically fine, but taking their money will doing it was not, and let\u2019s not mention it you vandalized a window, you soulless monster. The last house rule I had for revised was running entirely on just virtues, with obvious transgressions being contested against conscience/conviction where they either failed and gritted through it with artificial penalties, or they succeeded and felt bad about it. A roll came up fairly rare as they all kept to a moral compass they had set out. There was no chance of wassail, but if someone had wanted to play in such a struggle, I would have tailored the game to it. Degeneration with all its limits were really harsh as it was written, and with the artificial codes it did not do what it was supposed to do, and drained the fun out. So a really good change, easily moddable. <br /> <br /> But I think one of the best changes was to make combat etc contested rolls, instead of the sluggish attack/dodge circus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T02:39:04-07:00","id":1482912,"title":"","content":"1) As much as I loved the crunch of soak dices, they would slow down the game since you would have to roll everytime someone gets hit, maybe stamina could work like armor and nullify points of damage equal to its rate before all the damage get halved first, I know it's kinda of OP but V5 vamps are weakling so bumping them up a little couldn't hurt.<br /> <br /> 2) I like how the difficulty work, never been a fan of how it was handled in the old games, too much unnecessary math involved.<br /> <br /> 3) Thumbs down, in my opinion those are the worst mechanics of V5 so far, the idea in theory is cool but the execution is absolutely awful.<br /> <br /> 4) I have never been a fan of humanity in any of the vampire games (even requiem), it feels too gamey while it should be a personal aspect that should be discussed with the ST on a character basis since a college studend who just got turned will have a different outlook on what is right and wrong compared to an hardened criminal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T02:47:39-07:00","id":1482914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (1)Stamina giving health levels instead of soak dice. </div> </div> </div>Down <br /> While I actually homeruled and turned stamina and fortitude into automatic soak for vampires, rather than a roll, I like the old health track. It also helps me keep track if everyone has the same number of health levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (2)Difficulty being purely the number of 6+'s, rather than a combination of the difficulty being anything from 3+ to 10 and the number of successes. </div> </div> </div>Down.<br /> Feels too arbitrary. I don't know how much it is, but it doesn't feel right for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (3)The introduction of Hunger Dice and the resultant Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals. </div> </div> </div>Ultimately down.<br /> I like the idea that being hungry and the beast getting angrier about it makes it difficult to get things done, and I like the Atrocity Dice they were inspired by. What I don't like is the blood pool getting replaced and the randomness of V5's hunger system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (4)Humanity based around 3 sins rather than a 1-10 chart. </div> </div> </div>Brief up, as I enjoy making humanity about a vampire's personhood and will to keep going vs the unquenchable hunger, pain and despair inherent in the beast... followed by several thumbs down for the rest of V5's humanity system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T08:44:16-07:00","id":1482935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes#post1482849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(1)Stamina giving health levels instead of soak dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Down, people become Far too squishy. Ultimately this will agrivate the &quot;first strike&quot; problem VTM already has.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes#post1482849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(2)Difficulty being purely the number of 6+'s, rather than a combination of the difficulty being anything from 3+ to 10 and the number of successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd make thing simpler, but it also cuts out a lot of the gameplay and reders a Large number of discipline powers useless half the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes#post1482849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(3)The introduction of Hunger Dice and the resultant Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally had a thread about merging the V5 and V-classic systems, I suggest that over V5 straight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes#post1482849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(4)Humanity based around 3 sins rather than a 1-10 chart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thumbs down here. The paths and roads have that many sins to represent how its easy to fall if you're a good person, but harder to degenerate the lower you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T09:30:27-07:00","id":1482940,"title":"","content":"Thread OP feels kind of edition war bait to be honest. You gave no context for what you were wanting done, which is basically 'do you or don't you like these V5 mechanics'. And we have seen a lot of those threads devolve into some sort of edition war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T11:29:43-07:00","id":1482952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes?p=1482902#post1482902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you heard of the Path of Power and Inner Voice?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see most of them having the stomach for that path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T11:37:32-07:00","id":1482953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes?p=1482898#post1482898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so with better clarity on the desired feedback:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thumbs up. Good fit for the general change in combat mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also thumbs up. The older game had too many variables and something needs to go. Target numbers being set at X is the best of the options because it makes it much easier to understand the math of the game and how to value different adjustments. Needing to roll 7s instead of 6s for +1 dice of damage is not intuitive to understand if that's a good or bad deal. Taking a -1 dice penalty to inflict 1 damage is easier to see as, on average, a fairly good deal on average damage, but still tactically variable because of how V5 combat works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thumbs down. Hunger Dice are too present leading to Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals as too much of a constant risk regardless of the stakes of the scene. The justification the &quot;blood points are a boring gas tank,&quot; given by Martin I think loses both the utility of tracking set points over random outcomes,and how to connect the random outcomes effectively as consequence for other choices.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hard to answer as I don't entirely agree on the premise of treating the three Chronicle Tenets as equivalent to the old sins charts (there are other ways to get stains that apply regardless of Chronicle Tenets).<br /> <br /> But to give some level of answer to the intended comparison: thumbs up to negotiated for the group chronicle &quot;morality&quot; as a tool to help get the group on the same page as to the moral themes that will be present in a given instance, but thumbs down to the implementation and specifically of how it interacts with the Stains system. Most specifically I find the guidance on how severe a Stain penalty should be very lacking. Once you get to &quot;how bad is this violation&quot;as a ST, you have incredibly broad fiat to interpret and assign Stains for the action, and the players have to trust you to be fair and fun in it and have minimal recourse in the text regarding best practices to point to if they have trouble with the call.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second all that.<br /> <br /> I'm under the impression that some people that gave thumbs down did so in relation to the classic system instead of V5, so the OP is really badly phrased in this regard.<br /> <br /> All in all there is polishing to be made on V5 rules-wise (lore wise is beyond this thread), but those are mostly good changes.<br /> <br /> Hunger Dice may work if their use is better implemented, but as a constant feature of random problems arising at every action, not really useful. It could be a fixed penalty/bonus to some specific actions, or go into effect only at certain times. It could even derive some ideas from how Nightmare works in C20, which is a far better mechanic for a tangentially similar concept.<br /> <br /> Chronicle Tenets are in general a good idea and good implementation. But the Stains system needs a whole lot of tweaking and testing to properly polish it, so the Tenets are a good rule linked to a problematic system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T13:16:23-07:00","id":1482963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes?p=1482940#post1482940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thread OP feels kind of edition war bait to be honest. You gave no context for what you were wanting done, which is basically 'do you or don't you like these V5 mechanics'. And we have seen a lot of those threads devolve into some sort of edition war.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Then report it. Don't attempt to moderate yourself. This is threadcrapping.'</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T14:52:38-07:00","id":1482970,"title":"","content":"Depends what your goal is. Are you trying to make combat more survivable? Stamina = Health Levels is pretty much a universally bad idea. In almost every game I've ever played, damage mitigation (via dodge or soak) has trumped extra health every time. Indeed, there are builds in multiple games built solely around achieving near 100% Dodge or 100% Soak that sacrifice health to achieve it, and they were some of the most effective playstyles, to the point of dominating the meta. If you're looking for survivability, moving in that direction would be more efficient. <br /> <br /> Sins: Honestly, Humanity could probably be boiled down to &quot;Don't steal, don't vandalize, don't kill.&quot; That's what most characters lose humanity for. <br /> <br /> About the Hunger thing, I don't play V5 for reasons the Jannies on this forum won't allow to be discussed (despite community feedback possibly making the next iteration, you know, better) so I can't offer feedback there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T15:19:20-07:00","id":1482975,"title":"","content":"You can't look at Stamina as health levels without taking into account other changes to combat. In my opinion, it is a great change and reduces a lot of rolling.<br /> <br /> Fixed target number is also great, way easier to know your odds, and way easier to design homebrew around.<br /> <br /> Hunger complications have been really fun<br /> <br /> Humanity system is a massive improvement, though I echo that it should have been renamed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T16:17:48-07:00","id":1482986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes?p=1482970#post1482970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends what your goal is. Are you trying to make combat more survivable? Stamina = Health Levels is pretty much a universally bad idea. In almost every game I've ever played, damage mitigation (via dodge or soak) has trumped extra health every time. Indeed, there are builds in multiple games built solely around achieving near 100% Dodge or 100% Soak that sacrifice health to achieve it, and they were some of the most effective playstyles, to the point of dominating the meta. If you're looking for survivability, moving in that direction would be more efficient.<br /> <br /> Sins: Honestly, Humanity could probably be boiled down to &quot;Don't steal, don't vandalize, don't kill.&quot; That's what most characters lose humanity for.<br /> <br /> About the Hunger thing, I don't play V5 for reasons the Jannies on this forum won't allow to be discussed (despite community feedback possibly making the next iteration, you know, better) so I can't offer feedback there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP asks in the context of V5, so there is damage mitigation outside Stamina. This rule of Stamina going to Health Levels also exists in CoD, that also has standard defense without soak.<br /> <br /> So we could change the phrasing a bit to say &quot;change standard mitigation from Soak to Dodge&quot;, because that's the really difference here, pre-V5 WoD has soak because it doesn't has any standard defensive trait to reduce the attack pool, instead it requires complex extra decisions to make it happen.<br /> <br /> You don't need to like V5 as a whole, but I particularly think that this change in focus was good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T10:06:27-07:00","id":1483046,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...<br /> <br /> 1. Stamina as Health Levels I'm neutral on. It makes Stamina more valuable in one sense, while making it less valuable in another. Also, it requires rejigging all the damage numbers. So I can roll with it if done well. I personally like soak, though, and use fixed damage and soak values instead of dice pools. Works well so far.<br /> <br /> 2. Fixed target numbers are solid. I don't like how V5 did it, though. I think VTR2e's method is the most transparent (one die gives 0.33 successes), but it requires rerolling 10s to give a neat number (doubling 10s gives 0.4 successes per die, which is less neat). <br /> <br /> Exalted is my preferred fixed TN system, so you aim for 7+ and 10s double. Ignore 1s unless you fail. It works out that each die gives you 0.5 successes, on average.<br /> <br /> I also really dislike 'two 10s double' in V5. It just seems unintuitive. But if you had a botch system, and made botches happen on any failed roll with two 1s, I'd hate it less, because at least there's symmetry. It just stands out as this weird exception. Which leads me to...<br /> <br /> 3. I dislike BFs and MCs as they are implemented, but think they could be good. Personally, I'd make BFs much rarer (so you'd need to botch by failing and rolling two 1s, with at least one of those 1s rolled on a Hunger Die). <br /> <br /> MCs shouldn't be a thing, except on Disciplines or rolls where you Blood Surge, and I think you could probably make them an option for succeeding at a cost instead. Allow a PC to succeed if they take a messy complication on any partial success, scaling the complication according to however many successes short of the difficulty you were. In that way, the Beast pushes you through, at a cost.<br /> <br /> 4. I don't like this. I'd rather something like HTV's Integrity and Code. So you have three broad categories (Initiate, Adherent. Paragon), with each representing 1-3, 4-6 and 7-10.<br /> <br /> Paths allow you to intentionally violate a breaking point in order to switch it for one from your Path, at the risk of degeneration if it doesn't take.<br /> <br /> When you have replaced all your core Humanity breaking points with those from a Path, you can start increasing your rating again.<br /> <br /> This way, you only need three broad categories of sins, sins matter for longer (you don't fail it once and then ignore it, unless you take a Bane to strike it off or have an opportunity to replace it), switching to a Path is a clearer route, and you can always add in Tenets and Convictions as additional breaking points to flesh a character out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T10:18:42-07:00","id":1483049,"title":"","content":"1- Kill it<br /> 2-Kill it<br /> 3-Kill it<br /> 4-You'll need to elaborate further. The HOS is certainly flawed, but I'm not sure 3 rules/GM's opinion would be an improvement.<br /> <br /> Justifying myself a little:<br /> 1: This makes combat too lethal. First strike wins. There's little problems with soak as is. Just take Half rather than roll if you want to speed things up. Also I like tough vampries being &quot;impossible to hurt without enough umph due to supernatural sturdyness&quot; rather than just &quot;bigger HP bar&quot;. Feels more real. <br /> 2: V5 has a problem where you need lots of dice to do a &quot;normal&quot; action so yeah, nah, don't do this. Also you might as well not use d10s if you do this. <br /> 3: Hunger complications are antithetical to the idea of the Masquerade and phrase &quot;the Beast I am lest the Beast I become&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-04-2022, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T11:15:17-07:00","id":1483052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes#post1482849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(1)Stamina giving health levels instead of soak dice.<br /> <br /> (2)Difficulty being purely the number of 6+'s, rather than a combination of the difficulty being anything from 3+ to 10 and the number of successes.<br /> <br /> (3)The introduction of Hunger Dice and the resultant Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals.<br /> <br /> (4)Humanity based around 3 sins rather than a 1-10 chart.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1= Meh. I miss the stun if you receive damage double to your stamina.<br /> <br /> 2= Don't like. Feel like floping coins.<br /> <br /> 3= Thumbs down. Too intrusive.<br /> <br /> 4=Down. Mainly bc you need three people to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T11:21:38-07:00","id":1483054,"title":"","content":"The value of Stamina boosting Health instead of damage reduction, as noted by monteparnas, really needs to be looked at in relation to the rest of the rules.<br /> <br /> For example &quot;first strike wins,&quot; is a less of a thing in V5's mechanics by virtue of active defense being a contested roll where the winner (even if that's the defender) is the one that does damage. In most relatively even fights, combat is going to be a series of close rolls for minimal damage. This means higher health is a huge advantage, because a protracted exchange of generally even combatants is an attrition war... and more health means you start out with more of the resource in question.<br /> <br /> Building simply to &quot;not get hit&quot; in V5 is perfectly doable, but not optimal if you actually want to defeat opponents in combat. If you want to avoid fights at all costs? Sure. But then Stamina as soak vs. Stamina as health is a largely irrelevant point: Stamina isn't important to not getting hit in the first place, and either version is just extending how many times you can afford get hit before running away against someone that has a chance of hitting you. If you want to get hit as little as possible, and beat opponents in combat, you're maximizing your offensive roll to use as your attack roll or your active defense roll, and then we go back to my previous point.<br /> <br /> The big difference in the overall picture really falls on armor. If you look at the CofD or Storypath systems (consider that every ST based game is moving to the more Stamina = more Health model here), access to armor is still pretty essential for a &quot;tank&quot; build. A VtR 2e vampire with good armor can turn blows that would be fight ending to a mortal into ones that aren't even worth spending a bloodpoint on to heal; and the more health the less important it is for them to worry about healing mid-combat instead of using blood for other things and then feed later. V5 vampires gain virtually no practical benefit from armor (or a more different way to look at it could be that all V5 vampires are innately armored). The fact that wearing plate armor, or a modern ballistic vest with metal trauma plates, means nothing against a bunch of hunters trying to pepper you with wooden shafted crossbow bolts to stake you is the biggest issue in the &quot;dodge everything vs. tank&quot; effectiveness topic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T05:47:03-07:00","id":1483119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482849-thumbs-up-or-thumbs-down-these-mechanic-changes?p=1483054#post1483054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The value of Stamina boosting Health instead of damage reduction, as noted by monteparnas, really needs to be looked at in relation to the rest of the rules.<br /> <br /> For example &amp;quot;first strike wins,&amp;quot; is a less of a thing in V5's mechanics by virtue of active defense being a contested roll where the winner (even if that's the defender) is the one that does damage. In most relatively even fights, combat is going to be a series of close rolls for minimal damage. This means higher health is a huge advantage, because a protracted exchange of generally even combatants is an attrition war... and more health means you start out with more of the resource in question.<br /> <br /> Building simply to &amp;quot;not get hit&amp;quot; in V5 is perfectly doable, but not optimal if you actually want to defeat opponents in combat. If you want to avoid fights at all costs? Sure. But then Stamina as soak vs. Stamina as health is a largely irrelevant point: Stamina isn't important to not getting hit in the first place, and either version is just extending how many times you can afford get hit before running away against someone that has a chance of hitting you. If you want to get hit as little as possible, and beat opponents in combat, you're maximizing your offensive roll to use as your attack roll or your active defense roll, and then we go back to my previous point.<br /> <br /> The big difference in the overall picture really falls on armor. If you look at the CofD or Storypath systems (consider that every ST based game is moving to the more Stamina = more Health model here), access to armor is still pretty essential for a &amp;quot;tank&amp;quot; build. A VtR 2e vampire with good armor can turn blows that would be fight ending to a mortal into ones that aren't even worth spending a bloodpoint on to heal; and the more health the less important it is for them to worry about healing mid-combat instead of using blood for other things and then feed later. V5 vampires gain virtually no practical benefit from armor (or a more different way to look at it could be that all V5 vampires are innately armored). The fact that wearing plate armor, or a modern ballistic vest with metal trauma plates, means nothing against a bunch of hunters trying to pepper you with wooden shafted crossbow bolts to stake you is the biggest issue in the &amp;quot;dodge everything vs. tank&amp;quot; effectiveness topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. You either need Requiem's damage or StoryPath's if you want Stamina to add to HLs. Which has a knock-on effect for healing and things like that (e.g., VTR2e uses Strength to hit, and doesn't add Strength again to damage). <br /> <br /> V5's would also work, but you'd need better armour rules. V20's damage and armour won't work with Stamina adding HLs -- at least, not without lots more work.<br /> <br /> I'm drawn to narrative effects over HLs if you're going to change things up. StoryPath sort of does that, in a way, so that's another plus for that system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}